  "title": "Gavin M NDE",
  "date": "2025-01-07T15:21:20.000Z",
  "content": "I had no eyes so I saw nothing. I could feel; so, I knew I existed. I had the thought that I died and lost my wife and little boy.<br><br> But there was no sadness, only joy at the thought of no more material world and no more stress or worry. I was free. <br><br> I was space without any feeling of restriction. If I would have been in a room, I would have been the whole room.<br><br> I had a feeling there was something safe and familiar. Then I realized that I was with my grandmother. We could communicate, but without words. I just knew what she was thinking and she knew what I was thinking. We were both just space. She let me know that I shouldn't get comfortable because I wouldn't be staying long. I remember thinking that I wasn't going anywhere. I was free.<br><br> Next thing I know, I jump forward to waking up from a coma. My first thought was of Nan. I needed be with Nan, she still exists. Now, I'm not scared of death because I fully know that there is somewhere after this world. <br><br>",
